  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Call the numbers – round and hit",
  "description": "Two teams, each player with a ball. On each side stand three cones with a ball on top, numbered 1–3 going away from the lines. Blue run round the red cones and hit the blue balls, and red do the opposite.\n\nThe coach calls two numbers, for example \"2–1\": run round cone 2 on the far side, then hit ball 1 on your own side by passing at it. Put the ball back, dribble home and give the next player a high five. The first to hit it wins a point.\n\nSwitch the teams round so the turns are made with the other foot. Relay version: the teams go in order 1–1, 2–2, 3–3, and the first team to hit ten balls wins. Vary it with only the inside or only the outside of the foot in the turn.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Listen to both numbers before you go."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Small touches close to the cone and fast out of the turn."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Look up – the other player is coming towards you in the middle."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Pass with the inside of the foot and aim at the middle of the ball."
    }
  ],
